  "title": "Combined review pages can keep an approval that was dismissed between page reads",
  "file": "src/land/queue.ts",
  "A": {
   "verdict": "REAL",
   "failure_scenario": "Someone dismisses the only qualifying approval while the factory reads successive review pages. The factory combines the outdated approval with the remaining pages and merges without a current qualifying approval.",
   "reproduction": {
    "command": "bun test \"$TMPDIR/adjudicate-land.test.ts\" --test-name-pattern 'ADJ F[12]'",
    "output": "ADJ F1 {\"dismissed\":true,\"currentReview\":\"DISMISSED\",\"mergeCalls\":1,\"state\":\"landed\",\"graphqlReads\":3}\n2 pass, 0 fail"
   },
   "evidence": "The temporary integration test reused the HEAD land-queue fixtures and injected review pages with unchanged PR metadata. HEAD checks only headRefOid, state and isDraft across pages, then executes `reviews.push(...(seen.reviewEvidence ?? []))` and returns the accumulated reviews with `reviewEvidenceComplete: true`. It never revalidates the first page. Base had no approval-evidence pagination or approval gate."
  },
  "B": {
   "verdict": "REAL",
   "failure_scenario": "On a PR with more than 20 reviewers who approved or requested changes, the factory reads the review list in pages. If the only qualifying approval is dismissed in the short gap between reading page one and page two, the factory still counts it and merges the PR without a current approval.",
   "reproduction": "unreproduced: I did not build a multi-page fake transport. The mechanism is clear from the code quoted in evidence.",
   "evidence": "src/land/queue.ts:606-647 at head: `for (;;) { ... if (first && (seen.headRefOid !== first.headRefOid || seen.state !== first.state || seen.isDraft !== first.isDraft)) return {...incomplete}; first ??= seen; reviews.push(...(seen.reviewEvidence ?? [])); ... if (!hasNextPage) return { login, seen: { ...first, reviewEvidence: reviews, reviewEvidenceComplete: true } };` Reviews collected from earlier pages are never re-checked; only the head, PR state and draft flag are compared across pages. hasOtherApproval then trusts the combined list. It needs over 20 latest opinionated reviews plus a dismissal inside a gap of milliseconds to seconds, so it is unusual."
  }
 },
